.DS_Store
*.pkg

# Extracted binary data (too large for git, regenerable from gog/)
shared/data/u8-pkg-expanded/
shared/data/u8-install/
shared/data/extracted/
shared/data/lv-usecode/
shared/data/USECODE.FLX
shared/data/lv-usecode.zip
shared/data/discord/
MT32_*.ROM
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Large game binaries (not suitable for git)
gog/
scummvm-lv/
# Second ScummVM tree: the --enable-text-console build, whose debugger
# reads stdin. Same rationale as scummvm-lv/ above (large, regenerable,
# and it carries its own .git, so an unignored path commits a gitlink).
scummvm-lv-console/
shared/u8-lv-patched/

# Claude Code worktrees (embedded git repos, not tracked)
.claude/worktrees/

# Claude Code per-machine state. .claude/projects/ is keyed by absolute path,
# so a committed copy is dead weight on every other machine — one was tracked
# from 2026-05-20 to 2026-08-11 under a macOS path key that never matched
# again. Shared config (commands/, rules/, skills/) IS tracked; this is not.
.claude/projects/
CLAUDE.local.md

# The six MERGED game-data artifacts (M22, PLAN 4.3). Each is our work
# fused with Origin-copyrighted bytes we have no right to redistribute, so
# the repo must never carry them — rebuild from your own install with
# tools/build_artifacts.sh, which verifies against the tracked, byte-free
# shared/build/ARTIFACTS.sha256. (These were tracked until 2026-07-25; the
# history purge that removes them from past commits is planned in
# docs/history-purge-plan.md and must run before any visibility change.)
# ANIM.DAT joined them 2026-10-08 (the Tiny Tar body, shape 867) and was
# never tracked.
shared/build/ANIM.DAT
shared/build/EUSECODE.FLX
shared/build/GLOB.FLX
shared/build/FIXED.DAT
shared/build/TYPEFLAG.DAT
shared/build/U8SHAPES.FLX

# Same rationale, found during the M22 audit and missed by the review's
# inventory: a March-era prototype archive that is the base game's 42 maps
# plus one 122-item test map. No code reads it — only the map-builder
# devlogs mention it — and it is superseded by the real build.
shared/maps/FIXED_TEST.DAT

# Preview / scratch render output (regenerable, large)
shared/build/overlay/
shared/build/map_manifest.json
shared/build/map_previews/
shared/build/village_previews/
shared/build/shape_viewer.html
shared/build/previews/
# Build byproducts of the staged-write gates (P2 for EUSECODE.FLX, L12 for
# FIXED.DAT): a build writes <artifact>.staging, verifies it, then promotes
# it. A REJECTED build is quarantined as <artifact>.failed for inspection.
# MapArchive.save() also uses a unique <name>.<random>.staging temp file for
# write atomicity. None of these should ever be committed — .failed in
# particular is a known-corrupt artifact.
shared/build/*.staging
shared/build/*.failed
map_*.png
lv_run.log
